<h1>Smith-Waterman algorithm</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A means of searching protein databases to find those with the best alignment.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Aggregate child</strong> (... is a part of or used in me.)<br>
<a href="dynamicprog.html"><em>dynamic programming</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Ahmed Moustafa's implementation in <a href="http://jaligner.sourceforge.net/" target="_blank">JAligner (Java)</a>.
<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
<strong>Temple F. Smith</strong> and <strong>Michael S. Waterman</strong>, <em>Identification of Common Molecular Subsequences</em>, J. Mol. Biol., 147:195-197, 1981.
</p>

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

